#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:54
msgid "Each grouped dock title is a separate Tab stop. Its normal focus style marks the focused title (an underline in Cosmic Dusk); moving focus does not change the selected dock. Activate a title to switch docks and focus its first control. Clicking a dock tab also focuses its first control, even if that tab is already selected. Only the active dock's visible controls participate in the Tab sequence; hidden dock controls are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:61
msgid "When focus is inside a dock, the underline stays beneath its active tab. When you Tab between titles, the underline follows the focused title. The timeline itself is one Tab stop; Tab does not visit each clip or transition."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:65
msgid "The timeline's ruler and track headers, including their labels, dim when unfocused. The clip area stays the same. In Cosmic Dusk, a blue underline marks the focused dock's title text or active tab, and buttons show a blue focus border. The untitled timeline dock has no underline."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:71
msgid "Previewing a source"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:72
msgid "Press :kbd:`Shift+2` or :kbd:`Alt+P` with focus in Project Files to preview the selected file. With focus on the timeline, the same command previews the active selected clip from its Start point. With multiple items selected, the active selection anchor determines the source. Transitions and clips without an available project file do not open a source preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:78
msgid "An existing preview for the same file or the same timeline clip is reused. Different timeline clips have separate range-editing targets, even if they use the same source. When neither the file list nor the timeline has focus, the command does nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:83
msgid "In Preview File, click or drag the source ruler to scrub. Preview Clip and Split File also provide range editing: drag the Start/End grips, move the selected filmstrip range, draw a new range outside it, or edit their timecodes, or press :kbd:`I` / :kbd:`O` to set a marker at the playhead. End is the last included frame. :guilabel:`Loop` repeats the marked range. The preview uses your configured timeline playback and range-editing shortcuts: :kbd:`,` / :kbd:`.` move the range one frame (:kbd:`Shift` moves five). :kbd:`[` selects Start for trimming, :kbd:`]` selects End; comma and period then trim that edge. :kbd:`Esc` leaves trim mode before closing the dialog. :kbd:`Left` / :kbd:`Right` scrub frames without changing the range. :kbd:`Space` toggles playback, :kbd:`J` / :kbd:`L` change playback speed and :kbd:`K` pauses. These shortcuts leave text entry alone in Name and timecodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:96
msgid "Scrubbing and moving markers do not edit the project until you click the dialog's Create, Update, or Update Clip button. See :ref:`split_clip_ref`."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/keyboard.rst:100
msgid "Adding and applying assets"
